# The table editor, looks, lights, the camera and the screen layouts set by hand (tests/demo/pinball3d_editor_looks.sh), window
# 1440x900. The folder holds one image, art/deck.png. Things are taken by their names (Cmd+G), fields by their keys (Cmd+F).
# An upper playfield: its outline, four points, Enter.
4 key g meta
5 text +floor
6 key Enter
8 move 739 149
9 down
10 up
11 move 831 149
12 down
13 up
14 move 831 281
15 down
16 up
17 move 739 281
18 down
19 up
20 key Enter
# A look with a painting: "+look" adds one, its image is chosen among those of the folder; the upper playfield takes that look
# (chosen in the list of the table's looks by typing its name). Frame 52: the top view shows the painting on the upper playfield.
22 key g meta
23 text +look
24 key Enter
26 key f meta
27 text texture
29 move 1300 112
30 down
31 up
33 text deck
34 key Enter
36 key g meta
37 text floor1
38 key Enter
40 key f meta
41 text look
43 move 1300 112
44 down
45 up
47 text look1
48 key Enter
# The glow of a light: the light is taken by its name, and the round handle beside it on the top view is pulled away from it.
54 key g meta
55 text slingLight
56 key Enter
58 move 671 637
59 down
60 move 680 637
61 move 700 637
62 up
# A colour, picked: the swatch of the field opens the picker; a click in the square of shades sets it.
64 key g meta
65 text popCap
66 key Enter
68 key f meta
69 text color
71 move 1248 112
72 down
73 up
75 move 1380 160
76 down
77 up
# Another one, taken among the colours the table already uses (the fifth of them).
79 key f meta
80 text glow
82 move 1248 112
83 down
84 up
86 move 1299 316
87 down
88 up
# A click beside the board leaves the form; V shows the table in 3D. A drag in that pane turns the view round the table, and C keeps
# it: the layout the pane looks through (the portrait one: the pane is taller than wide) now looks at the table from there.
90 move 420 500
91 down
92 up
94 key v
98 move 900 450
99 down
100 move 880 460
101 move 860 480
102 up
104 key c
# The screen layouts take the place of the top view; the bonus of the landscape layout's panel is dragged to the left and down.
# Frame 120: the layout being edited.
106 key g meta
107 text layouts
108 key Enter
110 move 897 612
111 down
112 move 887 617
113 move 877 622
114 up
# Save.
122 key s meta
